treetMap","architecture_style":"Valabhi shikhara","construction_century":7},{"id":"8baf64ef-a5dd-4638-bca6-22dd5ba88321","name":"Prem Mandir, Vrindavan","deity":"Radha Krishna and Sita Ram","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Uttar Pradesh","district":"Mathura","town":"Sunrakh","latitude":27.57246,"longitude":77.67249,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Yamuna River","river_distance_km":1.7,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:36.374917+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Prem Mandir is a large temple complex on the outskirts of Vrindavan, set on about 22 hectares and founded by Kripalu Maharaj. Radha Krishna are enshrined on the first level and Sita Ram on the second, with a tribute to four earlier Jagadgurus beside the Sita Ram image.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Agra Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":53.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Vrindavan railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Prem Mandir, Vrindavan), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"8bdb1eda-a394-42c7-aec1-77c165575c90","name":"Mahalasa Narayani Temple, Mardol","deity":"Mahalasa, identified as Mohini, the female form of Vishnu","sampradaya":null,"significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Goa","district":"North Goa","town":"Mardol","latitude":15.441,"longitude":73.973,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Cumbarjua Canal River","river_distance_km":2.8,"best_season_notes":"Magha Jatra and Navaratri are the major festivals, with a Palakhi Seva on Sundays.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-26T20:05:50.919949+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"The present temple dates to the 17th century. The idol was rescued from the earlier temple at Verna, destroyed by the Portuguese in 1567. Tradition holds that the icon travelled from Nepal to Aurangabad and then to Goa — tradition, not documented history. Attendant shrines to Shantadurga and Lakshmi Narayan stand on the grounds.","etiquette_notes":"A tourism site says western or revealing clothing is prohibited; this is not from an official source.","native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Sources conflict and no official schedule was found (one lists roughly 9:30am–7:30pm, another 6:30am–8:30pm) — check locally.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Dabolim Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":28,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Karmali railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":7.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Mahalasa Narayani Temple, Mardol)","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":17},{"id":"8be717a3-0e95-4619-91a6-be0d8465e0fe","name":"Shiva Vishnu Temple, T. Nagar","deity":"Shiva and Vishnu","sampradaya":"Smartha","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Chennai","town":"T. Nagar","latitude":13.0415,"longitude":80.2335,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Adyar River","river_distance_km":1.9,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:51:40.218447+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Built in 1935, a joint Shiva-Vishnu shrine in the heart of T. Nagar, in the smarta tradition of housing both deities under one roof.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":8.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Mambalam railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Contributor-submitted local survey","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":20},{"id":"8c8ba1a2-8c44-40b5-ba2e-ba7a3fe761e4","name":"Alopi Devi Mandir, Prayagraj","deity":"Alopi Devi / Madhaveshwari (Devi)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":["Shakti Peetha"],"country":"India","state":"Uttar Pradesh","district":"Prayagraj","town":"Prayagraj","latitude":25.4451,"longitude":81.8712,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Ganga-Yamuna confluence","river_distance_km":2,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb; very crowded during the Magh Mela and Kumbh Mela years.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T11:10:03.827717+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-22T19:09:34.948917+00:00","sthala_purana":"Also called Prayaga Madhaveshwari, this Ashtadasha Shakti Peetha temple in the Alopi Bagh locality is unusual for having no murti at all. Tradition holds a fragment of Sati fell here and simply vanished (\"alop\") into the ground, so an empty wooden doli (palanquin cradle), draped in cloth and flowers, is worshipped in its place. A separate, more folk-historical account tells of a bride vanishing from her wedding doli near this spot.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"अलोपी देवी मंदिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Per tourism sources, not an official temple-board schedule: roughly 6am–10pm daily.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Prayagraj Airport (Bamrauli)","nearest_airport_distance_km":13,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Prayagraj Junction","nearest_railway_distance_km":6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Ashtadasha Shakti Peetha tradition; local oral history","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"8c9eb4dd-c0ca-430a-b8f0-6cbdfbc01c65","name":"Jyotirmath (Badari Peetham), Joshimath","deity":"Purna-giri / Narayana","sampradaya":"Smartha","significance":["Char Peetham"],"country":"India","state":"Uttarakhand","district":"Chamoli","town":"Joshimath","latitude":30.556,"longitude":79.5646,"sandhya_friendly":"yes","sandhya_notes":"The Alaknanda flows below the town, on the pilgrim route to Badrinath.","samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Alaknanda","river_distance_km":2,"best_season_notes":"May–Oct. Joshimath is the wintering seat for the Badrinath deity once the shrine closes for the season.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T13:44:40.752775+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"The northern Amnaya peetham, associated with the Atharva Veda. Its mahavakya is Ayamatma Brahma — \"this Self is Brahman\". Tradition holds that Adi Shankaracharya attained realisation here beneath a mulberry tree, and appointed his disciple Totakacharya to the seat.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ज्योतिर्मठ","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Dehradun Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":138.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":null,"nearest_railway_distance_km":null,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"8c9f36e0-b466-4257-ab67-772d8d0e7d61","name":"Subramaniya Swamy Temple, Thiruvidaikazhi","deity":"Murugan as Subramaniya Swamy","sampradaya":"Kaumara","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Mayiladuthurai","town":"Andur","latitude":11.04139,"longitude":79.78556,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Veeracholan River","river_distance_km":3.2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:56.940052+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Murugan temple in Thiruvidaikazhi, Mayiladuthurai district. According to tradition, Murugan's engagement to Deivanai took place here and he did penance after slaying the demon Hiranyasura. Murugan and Shiva are enshrined together in one sanctum, which is described as distinctive. The temple is mentioned in the Thevaram and Thiruppugazh hymns.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Neyveli Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":69.5,