,"town":"Tiruvallur","latitude":13.1425,"longitude":79.909,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kosasthalaiyar","river_distance_km":1,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:51:40.218447+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"Dated to around the 8th century, one of the 108 Divya Desams, the principal Vishnu temple of Tiruvallur town, roughly 8 minutes' drive from Thirumazhisai.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":32.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Tiruvallur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Contributor-submitted local survey; Nalayira Divya Prabandham","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":8},{"id":"8d4ad8a5-fb7a-48ac-b287-1e4b767f7cf2","name":"Baba Baijnath Temple, Agar","deity":"Shiva as Baba Baijnath","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Madhya Pradesh","district":"Agar Malwa","town":"Nipaniya Baijnath","latitude":23.73,"longitude":76.04,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Ahu River","river_distance_km":3.6,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:10:09.085477+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva temple in Agar, Madhya Pradesh. The article says it is believed to have been built by a British officer. Local people hold it in great faith and large crowds gather during festivals. The article mentions several interesting aspects associated with the temple.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Devi Ahilyabai Holkar Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":115,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Shajapur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":42.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Baba Baijnath Temple, Agar), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"8dfc3d59-a5ff-43ae-b611-4efc9c5ebc35","name":"Kedareswar Temple","deity":"Shiva as Kedareshwar","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Odisha","district":"Khordha","town":"Bhubaneswar Municipal Corporation","latitude":20.24217,"longitude":85.84031,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Dayaa River","river_distance_km":3.4,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:54.58588+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"One of the eight Astasambhu temples in Bhubaneswar, standing near Mukteswar and facing south. The sanctum has a sandstone yonipitha whose central linga is missing, and it sits below present ground level.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Biju Patnaik International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":3.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bhubaneswar railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Kedareswar Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"8e3e589f-4a60-40c8-8e84-a7af70121bd5","name":"Kedarnath Jyotirlinga","deity":"Shiva (Kedarnath)","sampradaya":null,"significance":["Jyotirlinga","Panch Kedar","Chota Char Dham"],"country":"India","state":"Uttarakhand","district":"Rudraprayag","town":"Kedarnath","latitude":30.7346,"longitude":79.0669,"sandhya_friendly":"yes","sandhya_notes":"Mandakini river runs alongside the temple town.","samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Kedarnath Mandir Samiti bhandara (seasonal, near the Alaknanda river crossing)","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Mandakini","river_distance_km":0.2,"best_season_notes":"Temple is open only late Apr/May to early Nov — closed and inaccessible in winter due to snow.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-05T20:00:08.393447+00:00","sthala_purana":"The Pandavas, seeking Shiva to be absolved of the killing of kinsmen at Kurukshetra, followed him to the Himalayas. Shiva took the form of a bull and dived into the ground; the hump remained at Kedarnath, and the other parts appeared at the four shrines of the Panch Kedar. As the site of the bull's hump, Kedarnath is reckoned the principal and most-visited of the five Panch Kedar shrines.","etiquette_notes":"The final stretch to Kedarnath (about 16-18km) is on foot, pony, palanquin, or helicopter — there is no road to the shrine itself. Warm layered clothing is essential even in the open season (late April/May to early November), as the temple sits above 3,500m.","native_name":"केदारनाथ ज्योतिर्लिंग","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":"The final 16-18km to the shrine has no road — reached on foot, pony, palanquin, or by helicopter (advance booking, weather-dependent). Not wheelchair-accessible. A genuine high-altitude trek, not a casual walk; altitude sickness is a real risk above 3,500m.","nearest_airport_name":"Dehradun (Jolly Grant) Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":235,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Rishikesh Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":210,"emergency_contact_notes":"Dial 112 for all-India emergency services. The route from Gaurikund has GMVN/police checkpoints and medical aid posts; register at the mandatory biometric checkpoint before starting the trek, which is also how rescue teams track pilgrims on the route.","sthala_purana_source":"Shiva Purana / Skanda Purana (Jyotirlinga tradition)","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"8ee2f1ec-989f-4d19-96f5-0eeb02d70930","name":"Ghaghar Burhi","deity":"Kali","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"West Bengal","district":"Paschim Bardhaman","town":"Asansol Kulti Township","latitude":23.6834,"longitude":87.0067,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Damodar River","river_distance_km":5.9,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:13:52.370722+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A small shrine to Goddess Kali in Asansol, West Bengal, beside the National Highway bypass. It is described as the oldest temple in the city. A country fair is held here on 15 January each year, and animal sacrifice is part of the worship.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kazi Nazrul Islam Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":24.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Kalipahari railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Ghaghar Burhi), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"8f0dd85a-aabf-4d9b-82b4-d1f4b7095b88","name":"Garh Ganesh Temple","deity":"Ganesha","sampradaya":"Ganapatya","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Rajasthan","district":"Jaipur","town":"Jaipur","latitude":26.94501,"longitude":75.82815,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Amanisha River","river_distance_km":3.1,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:10:09.085477+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Perched on the Aravalli hills near Jaipur, this temple is devoted to Ganesha. Its idol is unusual because it is shown without a trunk. It counts among the better-known religious sites of the city and draws many worshippers, particularly at Ganesh Chaturthi.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Jaipur International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":13,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Jaipur Junction railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":4.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Garh Ganesh Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"8f2840cc-94f2-413e-b9b6-9e558fa5539f","name":"Malleeswarar Temple, Mylapore","deity":"Malleeswarar (Shiva) / Maragathambal","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":["Saptha Sthana Mylapore"],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Chennai","town":"Mylapore, Chennai","latitude":13.0352,"longitude":80.2678,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Adyar River","river_distance_km":2.2,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T20:12:07.478318+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"One of the Saptha Sthana Sthalangal. Tradition holds a Shiva devotee named Prarthan came from Ayodhya and performed penance amid jasmine (malligai) bushes at this spot, and was granted darshan of Shiva with his consort Maragathambal — giving the shrine its name. The present temple dates to around the mid-18th century.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"மல்லீஸ்வரர் கோயில்","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":11.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Thirumayilai railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition (Saptha Sthana)","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":18},{"id":"8f6a830d-79c5-4477-b036-56de48fb7034","name":"Udayamperoor Ekadasi Perumthrikovil Temple","deity":"Shiva","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Kerala","district":"Ernakulam","town":"Udayamperoor","latitude":9.92036,"longitude":76.3612,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"thodupuzha yarr River","river_distance_km":0.9,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:13:52.370722+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"An ancient Shiva temple at Udayamperoor, Ernakulam, in Kerala style with monumental towers, a round sanctum and a courtyard of about four acres. Folklore credits Parashurama with installing the idol. It is one of the 108 Shiva temples of Kerala and has early inscriptions from the 12th and 13th centuries.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Cochin International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":26.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Chottanikkara Road railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Udayamperoor Ekadasi Perumthrikovil Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Kerala style with Kerala-Dravidian mukha mandapa","construction_century":12},{"id":"8f9294d1-5500-4610-b605-8bb543cb8973","name":"Makara Nedunkuzhaikathar Temple, Thenthiruperai","deity":"Makara Nedunkuzhaikathar (Vishnu)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["Nava Tirupati"],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Thoothukudi","town":"Thenthiruperai","latitude":8.603222,"longitude":77.986028,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Thamirabarani","river_distance_km":0.5,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T10:54:38.493897+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"One of the Nava Tirupati and a Divya Desam. Tradition holds that Bhoodevi (the earth goddess) performed penance here and discovered a pair of makara-shaped (crocodile-form) earrings, which Vishnu then wore — giving him the name Makara Nedunkuzhaikathar, \"he of the long makara earrings.\" Within the Nava Tirupati's parallel association with the nine planets, this shrine is linked to Shukra (Venus), and devotees pray here for relief from Venus-related afflictions.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"மகர நெடுங்குழைக்காதர் கோயில்","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Tuticorin Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":14.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Nazareth railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":4.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"8fa38180-b719-422d-8eb1-4150355373e0","name":"Adinatha Perumal Temple, Alwarthirunagari","deity":"Adinathar (Vishnu)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["Nava Tirupati"],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Thoothukudi","town":"Alwarthirunagari","latitude":8.607111,"longitude":77.938306,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Thamirabarani","river_distance_km":1,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Fe