,"town":"Bagribari (Pt)","latitude":26.2143,"longitude":90.1185,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Tipkai","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:53.924452+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"A major Shakta pilgrimage temple of Lower Assam near Bilasipara, regarded as second only to Kamakhya for visitors. The goddess was traditionally worshipped by local Kachari, Koch and Nath communities. The article notes a long tradition of animal sacrifice at Durga Puja, and a related bathing-ghat shrine on the Tipkai river.","etiquette_notes":"Animal sacrifice is traditionally performed, especially at Durga Puja.","native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Rupsi Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":22.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bagribari railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Mahamaya Dham), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"90ee0414-2551-4691-8a73-2b29034bcb6c","name":"Mehandipur Balaji Temple","deity":"Balaji (Hanuman)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Rajasthan","district":"Dausa","town":"Mehandipur","latitude":26.8833,"longitude":76.6667,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Banganga River","river_distance_km":10.8,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb, avoiding peak Rajasthan summer heat.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T17:30:52.99453+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Tradition holds the temple's Hanuman idol, worshipped here as Balaji (\"child Hanuman\"), manifested on its own in these Aravalli hills rather than being carved by any sculptor. The temple has become widely known specifically for rituals believed to relieve those affected by evil spirits or negative energies, drawing pilgrims from across North India seeking this kind of spiritual relief.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"मेहंदीपुर बालाजी मन्दिर","morning_opens_at":"04:00:00","morning_closes_at":"12:00:00","evening_opens_at":"16:00:00","evening_closes_at":"21:30:00","timings_notes":"Reported hours vary noticeably across sources — confirm locally, especially around the busy Tuesday/Saturday darshan.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Jaipur International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":84.3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bandikui Junction railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":20,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"910959c3-d3ad-4d13-a089-8e5d60b7666e","name":"Govindaraja Swamy Temple, Tirupati","deity":"Govindaraja (Vishnu), reclining in yoga-nidra and facing east","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Tirupati","town":"Tirupati","latitude":13.68325,"longitude":79.34719,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Papavinasa Kona River","river_distance_km":5.4,"best_season_notes":"Brahmotsavam and Vaikuntha Ekadasi are the major occasions.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-26T20:40:38.920003+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Consecrated in 1130 CE by Ramanujacharya (the temple's official site and Wikipedia agree), with some structures inside dated to the 9th–10th centuries; Parthasarathy was the earlier presiding deity. Sources describe the ritual tradition variously as Vaikhanasa, with Vadakalai worship and Tenkalai influence — the affiliation is contested, so it is not narrowed further. The seven-storey rajagopuram (about 50 m) is attributed to Matla Anantaraja. Administered by the Tirumala Tirupati Devasthanams.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Tirupati Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":null,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Tirupati Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Govindaraja Temple, Tirupati); Tirupati district site","architecture_style":"Dravidian; seven-storey rajagopuram with Ramayana scenes and two enclosures","construction_century":12},{"id":"91740c2a-f4f0-44e4-bd2b-47068131119f","name":"Mukhalingam Temples (Madhukeshwara)","deity":"Shiva, as Madhukeshwara (Mukhalingeswara), with a faceted linga; the group includes Someswara and Bhimeswara temples","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Srikakulam","town":"Mukhalingam","latitude":18.6,"longitude":83.9667,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Vamsadhara","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-26T20:40:38.920003+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"Mukhalingam, on the left bank of the Vamsadhara, was historically Kalinganagari, capital of the Eastern Gangas from the 6th to the 12th century until the capital moved to Cuttack in 1122. Scholars date the temples to between the late 8th and early 11th century, and the dating is contested, so no single century is given. Patronage of the principal temple is credited to Kamarnava Deva II. Coordinates are village-level.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Alluri Sitarama Raju International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":84.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Tilaru railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":18.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Mukhalingam)","architecture_style":"Kalinga architecture","construction_century":null},{"id":"92262da4-6417-4620-b5d0-03039463fe2f","name":"ISKCON Temple, Delhi","deity":"Radha Parthasarathi (Krishna and Radha)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Delhi","district":"South Delhi","town":"Delhi","latitude":28.55806,"longitude":77.24333,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Yamuna River","river_distance_km":4.7,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:36.374917+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Sri Sri Radha Parthasarathi Mandir, known as the ISKCON Temple Delhi, is dedicated to Krishna and Radha as Radha Parthasarathi. It stands at Hare Krishna Hills near Nehru Place in East of Kailash, and was inaugurated on 5 April 1998 by then Prime Minister Atal Bihari Vajpayee.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Indira Gandhi International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":14.3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Okhla railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (ISKCON Temple, Delhi), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":20},{"id":"929ab21f-f0b0-4f7a-8abc-649cd7408438","name":"Ulagalandha Perumal Temple, Singanallur","deity":"Vishnu as Ulagalandha Perumal","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Coimbatore","town":"Singanallur","latitude":10.9968,"longitude":77.0305,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Noyyal River","river_distance_km":1.3,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:13:52.370722+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Vaishnavite temple in Singanallur, Coimbatore, also called Three Vikrama Narayana Swamy temple. The north-facing panchaloha main image stands with one leg raised and has eight hands, six carrying weapons. Worship follows the Pancharatra Agama. It is said to have been built about 180 years ago, with renovation in 2000 and a kumbabhishekam in 2005.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Coimbatore International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":4.3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Singanallur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Ulagalandha Perumal Temple, Singanallur), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"92d3bf36-0793-48c1-a597-68cd2f0333e9","name":"Siddhanath Temple, Mhaswad","deity":"Shiva as Siddhanath","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Maharashtra","district":"Satara","town":"Mhasvad","latitude":17.63111,"longitude":74.7875,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Manganga River","river_distance_km":0.2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:36.374917+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"This temple at Mhaswad in Maharashtra honours Siddhanath, regarded as a form of Shiva and one of the regional protector (Kshetrapal) deities of the state. The town is known for its yearly Mhaswad Yatra fair, during which devotees are covered in pink gulal and pull a chariot of the deity.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Solapur Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":121.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Wasud railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":47.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Siddhanath Temple, Mhaswad), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"935fa06e-f906-47b8-af28-dc0e942c380e","name":"Bathu Temples","deity":"Shiva and Parvati","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Himachal Pradesh","district":"Kangra","town":"Dehra","latitude":32.04724,"longitude":76.00365,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Buhal Khad River","river_distance_km":0.5,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:47.875457+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Known locally as Bathu ki ladi, this is a cluster of temples in Kangra district, Himachal Pradesh, with the main shrine for Parvati and Shiva. The temples were submerged in the Maharana Pratap Sagar reservoir after the Pong dam was built in the early 1970s, and can be reached only from May to June when the water level falls.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Accessible only from May to June when the reservoir level drops, according to the article.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kangra Airport, Gaggal","nearest_airport_distance_km":27.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Harsar Dehri railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":7.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Bathu Temples), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"936725b6-8b3e-46ba-a1f9-5ad7816f7b0e","name":"Nilkanth Mahadev","deity":"Shiva as Nilkanth","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Uttarakhand","district":"Pauri Garhwal","town":"Neelkanth Mahadev","latitude":30.0807,"longitude":78.3409,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Pankaja and Madhumati (confluence)","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:44.755986+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva temple about 32 km from Rishikesh in Pauri Garhwal, built in the Dravidian style. It is a well-known pilgrimage site set amid dense forest, between the Manikoot, Brahmakoot and Vishnukoot valleys, next to the Nar-Narayan ranges, at the meeting point of the Pankaja and Madhumati rivers.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Dehradun Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":19.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Rishikesh railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":5.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Nilkanth Mahadev), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Dravidian","construction_century":null},{"id":"93774367-f3de-409b-9c08-1913caee3d41","name":"Nameswara Temple, Pillalamarri","deity":"Shiva as Nameswara","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Telangana","district":"Suryapet","town":"Pillalamarri","latitude":17.16916,"longitude":79.58476,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Musi","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","v