Rama and Krishna. Devotees come from afar on Janmashtami.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Open 5:30 AM to 11 AM and 4:30 PM to 9 PM, according to the article.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Netaji Subhash Chandra Bose International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":16.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Ballygunge Junction railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Birla Mandir, Kolkata), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"99b2d725-4016-4822-b8bf-7e86dec6ecf7","name":"Pattadakal Group of Monuments","deity":"Shiva, across several temples; one Jain shrine","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Bagalkot","town":"Pattadakal","latitude":15.95139,"longitude":75.81472,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Malaprabha River","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T09:54:32.209521+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"A complex of 7th–8th century CE Hindu and Jain temples on the west bank of the Malaprabha, about 23 km from Badami and 9.7 km from Aihole. It is a UNESCO World Heritage Site and an ASI-protected monument. UNESCO describes it as a harmonious blend of northern and southern Indian architectural forms. The Hindu temples are generally dedicated to Shiva, with Vaishnava and Shakta elements, and their friezes depict episodes from the Ramayana, Mahabharata and Bhagavata Purana; the one Jain temple is dedicated to a single Jina.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Hubballi Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":102.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Guledgudda Road railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":18.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Pattadakal)","architecture_style":"Early Chalukya, blending northern (Nagara) and southern (Dravida) forms; ASI-managed UNESCO site","construction_century":8},{"id":"9a01691a-0a58-4661-ab76-dec20ce8cc7c","name":"Naimisharanya","deity":"Vishnu (Naimishnath)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Uttar Pradesh","district":"Sitapur","town":"Naimisharanya","latitude":27.3333,"longitude":80.4667,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Gomti River","river_distance_km":0.8,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb; Kartik Purnima draws especially large crowds for bathing at Chakratirtha.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T17:30:52.99453+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Tradition holds this forest was chosen by Brahma himself as the most sacred place for meditation in the Kali Yuga, after his discus (chakra) came to rest here at what is now the Chakratirtha pond. It is held to be where sage Vyasa first arranged the Vedas and Puranas, and where Suta Goswami later narrated all eighteen Puranas to an assembly of 88,000 rishis — making it one of the most textually significant sites in the Puranic tradition, alongside its many shrines including a Shakti Peetha to Lalita Devi.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_