 nine planets. The temple preserves roughly 1,100 years of Dravidian temple heritage.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"அம்மைநாதர் கைலாசநாதர் கோயில்","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Tuticorin Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":50.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Cheranmahadevi railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition (Agastya-Romasa Muni legend)","architecture_style":"Dravidian","construction_century":null},{"id":"9e3b9087-3b79-43cd-b279-f6b76b0d6261","name":"Alampur Navabrahma Temples","deity":"Shiva","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Telangana","district":"Jogulamba Gadwal","town":"Bhairanpalle","latitude":15.87781,"longitude":78.13483,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Tungabhadra","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T10:59:23.880063+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"Nine early Badami Chalukya temples of the 7th-9th centuries at Alampuram, Telangana, near the meeting of the Tungabhadra and Krishna rivers. Despite the Brahma name, they are dedicated to Shiva. They have square east-facing plans and carvings of Shaiva, Vaishnava and Shakta themes. The Archaeological Survey has restored them since 1980.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Uyyalawada Narasimha Reddy Airport ,   Kurnool","nearest_airport_distance_km":18.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Alampur Road railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":9.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Alampur Navabrahma Temples), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Early Badami Chalukya, Nagara","construction_century":7},{"id":"9e44d455-3c95-4fe2-b75f-eceb786f2c89","name":"Tanot Mata Temple","deity":"Tanot Mata","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Rajasthan","district":"Jaisalmer","town":"Tanot","latitude":27.79839,"longitude":70.35446,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:54.58588+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple in Jaisalmer district, Rajasthan, near the Pakistan border close to the Longewala battle site of 1971. Local folklore credits the goddess with that victory. She is held to be an incarnation of Hinglaj Mata and is worshipped as a goddess of war.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Jaisalmer Air Force Station","nearest_airport_distance_km":113,"nearest_railway_station_name":null,"nearest_railway_distance_km":null,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Tanot Mata Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"9e515d5e-3075-4e27-a2ef-354018ac868c","name":"Ballaleshwar Temple, Pali","deity":"Ballaleshwar (Ganesha)","sampradaya":"Ganapatya","significance":["Ashtavinayak"],"country":"India","state":"Maharashtra","district":"Raigad","town":"Pali","latitude":18.2333,"longitude":73.2333,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Ghod Madgaon River","river_distance_km":3.6,"best_season_notes":"Ganesh Chaturthi (Aug–Sep) is the busiest day; Oct–Feb otherwise for the Ashtavinayak circuit.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T13:05:55.016033+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Named after Ballal, a young devotee whose intense devotion to Ganesha so alarmed his father that he tried to stop it; Ganesha saved Ballal and stayed on as \"Ballaleshwar\" — the only Ashtavinayak temple named after a devotee rather than the deity's own form.","etiquette_notes":"Men are asked to wear a dhoti to perform puja inside the inner sanctum, per temple-visit guides — not confirmed against an official temple-trust source.","native_name":"श्री बल्लाळेश्वर मंदिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Reported as 5:30am–10pm by a travel site; not corroborated by an official source.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Pune International Airport (Lohegaon)","nearest_airport_distance_km":null,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Karjat railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":30,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"maharashtratourism.gov.in (Ashtavinayak, Pali)","architecture_style":"Peshwa-era Maratha temple architecture, built in the shape of the Devanagari letter \"Shri\"; the original wooden shrine was later replaced with the present stone structure","construction_century":null},{"id":"9f136c88-2d56-483e-a3fe-ba53f5ede7e5","name":"Vishvanatha Temple, Khajuraho","deity":"Shiva as Vishvanatha","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Madhya Pradesh","district":"Chhatarpur","town":"Khajuraho","latitude":24.8533,"longitude":79.92261,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Khudar River","river_distance_km":1.9,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:59.639499+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Part of the western group of Khajuraho monuments, a UNESCO World Heritage site, this temple honours Shiva as Lord of the Universe. It is believed to have been commissioned by the Chandela king Dhanga and was probably finished around 999 or 1002 CE. Its style resembles the Lakshmana and Kandariya Mahadeva temples, and it carries sculptures of deities, celestial maidens and mythical beasts.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Khajuraho Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":4.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Khajuraho railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":7.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Vishvanatha Temple, Khajuraho), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Chandela","construction_century":10},{"id":"9f354dea-5e4f-46eb-942b-57df4a4afa73","name":"Kothanda Ramar Temple, West Mambalam","deity":"Kothanda Ramar (Rama)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Chennai","town":"West Mambalam","latitude":13.0365,"longitude":80.22,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"sami