e","architecture_style":"Dravidian","construction_century":null},{"id":"a231d44d-51c1-4916-bb88-9030af8edc5c","name":"Raja Rajeshwara Temple, Vemulawada","deity":"Rajarajeshwara (Shiva)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Telangana","district":"Rajanna Sircilla","town":"Vemulawada","latitude":18.4167,"longitude":78.8833,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Maneru River","river_distance_km":0.5,"best_season_notes":"Feb–Mar for Maha Shivaratri, when the temple draws over half a million pilgrims.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T13:57:28.972216+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Built between the 11th and 12th centuries under a governor of the Kalyani Chalukyas, in what had earlier been the capital of the Vemulawada Chalukya dynasty (750–973 CE). Locally called Rajanna, the deity is enshrined alongside Raja Rajeshwari Devi and Siddhi Vinayaka. Tradition holds Shiva chose to make Vemulawada his home after residing at Kashi, Chidambaram, Srisailam, and Kedarnath, and that Indra worshipped here and bathed in the temple's Dharma Gundam tank after defeating the demon Vritrasura.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"వేములవాడ రాజరాజేశ్వర ఆలయం","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Ramagundam Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":62.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Sircilla railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":5.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"a248bd43-6dab-489d-a8a4-07e696c089a5","name":"Nilamadhav Temple","deity":"Vishnu as Nilamadhava","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Odisha","district":"Nayagarh","town":"Kantilo","latitude":20.36463,"longitude":85.1951,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Mahanadi","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:59.639499+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"An old Vishnu temple at Kantilo near the Mahanadi, close to twin hills and forest. A continuous flow of water from the deity's feet is a noted feature, and Lord Siddheswar is also present. Nilamadhava holds a central place in the Jagannath tradition, and his shrine stands beside the Lakshmi temple at Puri.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Biju Patnaik International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":65.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bolagarh Road railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":21.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Nilamadhav Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"a24985d7-1011-45b5-832c-b53ff5079685","name":"Raghunatha Temple, Alangiri","deity":"Raghunatha (Rama)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"West Bengal","district":"Purba Medinipur","town":"Egra-I","latitude":21.84659,"longitude":87.46926,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:10:09.085477+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"A large nine-spired (nava-ratna) temple at Alangiri near Egra, established in 1810 by the Das family. It rises from a high plinth inside the family courtyard, has triple-arched verandahs on three sides, and is about 40 feet tall, among the biggest in Midnapore.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Netaji Subhash Chandra Bose International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":134.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Ramnagar railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":20.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Raghunatha Temple, Alangiri), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Nava-ratna","construction_century":19},{"id":"a26315b1-d395-4894-903f-64722e149526","name":"Shanta Durga Temple","deity":"Shantadurga (Durga)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Goa","district":"South Goa","town":"Ponda","latitude":15.39583,"longitude":73.96777,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Cumbarjua Canal River","river_distance_km":5.3,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:20.030396+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"This temple stands at the foot of Kavalem village in Ponda Taluka, Goa, about 30 km from Panaji. Shantadurga is the family deity of many Goud Saraswat Brahmins, and the Swamiji of Kavale Math is the spiritual head of the temple trust. In 2016 the devasthan marked 450 years of existence.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Goa International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":14.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Verna railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":7.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Shanta Durga Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"a2d703d0-d033-4a2d-9e52-ddee0823f6c7","name":"Unakoti, Tripura","deity":"Shiva, in the form of Unakotiswara Kal Bhairava (a rock-cut figure about 30 ft tall), with Ganesha, Durga and Nandi","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tripura","district":"Unakoti","town":"Kailashahar","latitude":24.3167,"longitude":92.0667,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Manu River","river_distance_km":6.1,"best_season_notes":"The Ashokastami Mela in April is the main fair, with a smaller one in January.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-26T20:05:50.919949+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Legend says Shiva halted here on his way to Kashi with one crore minus one deities, who overslept and were cursed into stone. Local tribal tradition instead credits the sculptor Kallu Gurjar, who was set to carve a crore images in a night and fell one short. The dating is contested: the district administration suggests the 7th–9th century \"if not earlier\", while the one known inscription is in Bengali characters of the 11th–12th century. Coordinates are approximate.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Agartala Airport (Maharaja Bir Bikram)","nearest_airport_distance_km":178,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Kumarghat Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":26,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Unakoti district site; Wikipedia (Unakoti)","architecture_style":"Rock-cut and rock-relief sculpture","construction_century":null},{"id":"a33a0279-a12c-4089-aee0-3fdb52778b85","name":"Ubaya Rameswara Kshetram","deity":"Shiva as Rameswara, with Parvati","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Bapatla","town":"Sugguna Lanka","latitude":16.23134,"longitude":80.78751,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Krishna","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:54.58588+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva and Parvati temple at Chilumuru in Bapatla district, Andhra Pradesh, on the Krishna River. The main deity is a lingam made of sand, said by the sthala purana to have been set up by Sita. The riverbank draws bathers at Maha Shivaratri and Karthika.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Vijayawada Airport","nearest_airport_distance_