arpur","latitude":17.6792,"longitude":75.3324,"sandhya_friendly":"partial","sandhya_notes":"Chandrabhaga river ghat is close but very crowded during Wari/Ekadashi; quieter on regular weekdays.","samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Pandharpur Devasthan pure-veg canteen","food_source_contact":"+91-217-232-2100","food_distance_km":0.6,"nearest_river_name":"Chandrabhaga (Bhima)","river_distance_km":0.3,"best_season_notes":"Avoid Ashadhi and Kartiki Ekadashi (Wari season) unless you specifically want the pilgrimage crowd experience.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-05T19:02:16.315601+00:00","sthala_purana":"The sthala purana relates that Vitthal came to Pandharpur for his devotee Pundalik, who was serving his aged parents and tossed out a brick for the waiting god to stand upon. Vitthal is still shown standing on that brick, hands on hips, waiting — the posture in which the Warkari tradition knows him.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"विठ्ठल रुक्मिणी मन्दिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Pune Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":200,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Pandharpur Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":"Hemadpanti; the original Hoysala-era shrine was destroyed and the present structure rebuilt in the 16th century","construction_century":16},{"id":"a3eb2d6f-ad65-4578-98a3-e606fba8f811","name":"Siddhanath Temple, Nemawar","deity":"Shiva as Siddheshwar","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Madhya Pradesh","district":"Dewas","town":"Khategaon Tahsil","latitude":22.4931,"longitude":76.978,"sandhya_friendly":"